## Approach
 1st and last element will always be 1.
 2nd element of any row in pascal's triangle will be (row - 1).
 Make sure to handle Edge case of row = 1

## Solution
```csharp[]
class Solution
{
    public int[] pascalTriangleII(int r)
    {
        if (r == 1)
            return new int[] {1};

        int[] answer = new int[r];
        answer[0] = 1;
        answer[r - 1] = 1;

        //2nd element of triangle will always have the value of r -1
        answer[1] = r - 1;
        int result  = answer[1];

        for (int i = 2; i < r - 1; i++) 
        { 
            result *= (r - i);
            result /= i;
            answer[i] = result;
        }      

        return answer;
    }   
}
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
Time Complexity will be O(N - 3) for N >= 3 where N is the length of row. For N = 1, 2 it will be O(1). 
Overall time complexity ~ O(N).

**Space Complexity:**
Auxilary space complexity is O(1)

